          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ஆட்சேபி — āṭcēpi — \"to object\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அந்த முடிவை யாரும் ஆட்சேபிக்கவில்லை. anta muṭivai yārum āṭcēpikkavillai. Nobody objected to that decision."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ஆட்சேபித்தேன், āṭcēpittēṉ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is objected to takes -ஐ: முடிவை ஆட்சேபி (āṭcēpi). The noun is ஆட்சேபனை, an objection."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ஆட்சேபி (āṭcēpi) is a verb built on Sanskrit ākṣepa, \"objection\" (CDIAL 1032). Tamil writes the Sanskrit kṣ as ட்ச, as in சாட்சி from sākṣin."
            }
          ]
        },
